  "title": "Conquest of Mecca",
  "summary": "In the eighth year of the Hijra Muhammad led an army of about ten thousand into Mecca after the truce with Quraysh broke down. Traditional accounts describe a city taken with little bloodshed, a general amnesty, and the removal of idols from the Kaaba. These details come from Muslim tradition, and sources differ on the exact date, around December 629 or January 630 CE.",
